Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

The signing is a checksum, not a signature
------------------------------------------

A vote is signed with FNV-1a over its payload and the voter's key. That catches a mangled or edited payload
and it is NOT a cryptographic signature: there is no secret-key exchange, no protection against someone who
knows the key, and no defence against a determined forger.

Do not use this app for anything that needs real cryptographic guarantees. It is a room-sized tally with a
root two devices can compare — nothing more.

What the root does
------------------

The root is a hash over the vote payloads in sorted order, so any two devices holding the same votes compute
the same eight characters. Flip one vote and the root changes; that is the check, and it is a check anyone in
the room can repeat by hand.

No camera
---------

There is no QR scanner and no camera in this app. A payload is a single line of text — the string a QR would
carry — and you move it however you like.
